      "side": 1,
      "message": "Andrew, Jiyong: Can you help with the build question here?\nWe want a library which exposes a simple C function API (so it can be called from C/C++ as if it was an NDK library) and can also be called from Rust. And the library itself is implemented in Rust.\n\nThe library implementation should be opaque to clients, so I wonder if we need a bindgen wrapper to call the C API via ffi from Rust (even though that seems fairly silly).",
      "revId": "6614d9c8ed501098d188a0d057979e481e4716b1",
