      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T11:15:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "using a rust_library with `prefer_rlib: true` makes a static linking.\n\nI don\u0027t think we need rust_library_dylib either because a dylib in general doesn\u0027t have a stable ABI. I think what you want is a rust wrapper for libvm_payload.so. The wrapper could be statically linked to the payload as an rlib.",
      "parentUuid": "3f9becb6_73a26325",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "6614d9c8ed501098d188a0d057979e481e4716b1",
